title: D219: The driver reads a program as native's load does:
status: closed
priority: medium
created: 2026-10-09T00:00:00Z
issue_type: decision
labels: llvm
external_ref: D219
description: The driver reads a program as native's load does: in `user`, then from each top-level `ns` or `in-ns` form on in the namespace it names, so `::k` is the program's own keyword on every target. It read the whole file in its own `driver` namespace before, so `::k` was `:driver/k` on both lanes (and in a program with its own `ns` form). `read-program` reads the file once, and a file that switches namespace is re-read from each switch, padded so each form keeps its `:line` and `:column`. The re-read consumes extra gensyms in such programs, so their GC output renumbers with no change in behavior (the guard re-freezes, D221). Still not as native: line 1's columns are one high (the reader's `[` wrapper, as before), and `::alias/k` resolves no alias. P1.10 runs `corpus/reader-ns` against native on both lanes.
